| `tests/integration/test_ci_pipeline_gate.py` | Fails a CI adapter that does not run config/project.json `ci_pipeline.steps` exactly, in order: a step dropped, added, reordered or changed, a changed or lost env value, an env word alone on its line (bash passes it to no command), a missing marker line, and for GitLab a compared key that the `.gitlab-ci.yml` keel ships lacks, sets otherwise, or sets and the file lacks, so the image must be `ci_pipeline.gitlab_image` filled from `toolchain` and `GIT_DEPTH` must be `"0"`. The GitLab judge guards whether keel's `test` job runs and exactly what it runs, never where it runs or what else the project runs. It compares with keel's file the `test` job, the top-level keys GitLab applies to every job (`after_script`, `before_script`, `cache`, `default`, `image`, `include`, `services`, `variables`, `workflow`), and any other top-level key the `test` job reads through a YAML anchor or merge, `extends` or `!reference`; every other top-level key, `stages` or a job or hidden job only the project's own jobs read, is the project's own and is not compared. In the `test` job, `interruptible`, `retry`, `stage`, `tags` and `timeout` may be set, `image` may take the long form `{name: ...}` naming the same image, and every other key, `rules`, `when`, `needs`, `allow_failure`, `variables` and `script` among them, is compared. A variable compares as GitLab reads it: a number is its string, so `GIT_DEPTH: 0` equals `"0"`. The GitLab file is read with a YAML parser, so a quoted or explicit key reads as itself and a key set twice is a fault naming both lines, and the `script` may be one string or a block or flow list; an empty step list and a tree with no adapter are faults, never a pass. In a project, the `ci_pipeline` answer, read with the YAML parser copier uses and a second `ci_pipeline` key a fault, picks what is judged: each chosen adapter, which must exist, and an unchosen one only when it carries the marker. | `make test` | [`ci_pipeline.steps`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`ci_pipeline.adapters`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`ci_pipeline.gitlab_image`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`ci_pipeline.marker`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Compares the files, not a run: it proves each adapter names the steps, not that a GitLab runner or the configured image can run them. A GitHub job-level `if:` or a changed `on:` is not judged yet (KEEL-CIGATE-1). Not the install sources an install step takes: `tests/integration/test_install_sources_gate.py` judges those. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
